# editor backup files
*~

# legacy C source (tcb/) build artifacts
tcb/src/*.o
tcb/src/*.P
tcb/*.P
# The built binary itself, under whatever name `make PROG=<name>` was
# given (2026-08-05: Makefile's own PROG variable, default "usilic" --
# see its own comment) -- "tcb"/"tcb.exe" kept for any build that
# didn't override PROG, "usilic" for this checkout's own actual use.
tcb/src/tcb
tcb/src/tcb.exe
tcb/src/usilic
# "U" (2026-08-25): src/config.sh's own PROGNAME, renamed from "usilic"
# so this legacy build installs alongside the C++ port (src/cpp/, which
# now owns the "usilic" name) without colliding -- see config.sh's own
# comment. "usilic" above is kept too, for any older checkout/build
# that hasn't re-run config.sh yet.
tcb/src/U
tcb/src/config.h
tcb/src/config.h.old
# progname.h is generated fresh by every `make` invocation (see
# Makefile's own progname.h rule) -- never hand-edited, never
# committed. tcb/src/Makefile itself is NOT listed here (2026-08-05):
# it's the genuine, hand-maintained source of truth for the PROG
# parameterization, not a locally-generated artifact -- see CLAUDE.md.
tcb/src/progname.h
tcb/src/progname.h.old
tcb/src/Makefile.old
tcb/src/.config
tcb/src/TAGS
tcb/src/t
tcb/src/TCB.EXE.stackdump
tcb/src/debug/

# perl scratch/doc build output (legacy C docs toolchain)
tcb/perl/tcb.dvi
tcb/perl/tcb.log
tcb/perl/tcb.aux
tcb/perl/t
tcb/perl/u
tcb/perl/s

# src/: config.sh output, C++ port build artifacts, generated man page
src/install.sh
src/.config
src/doc/tcb.1.gz
src/cpp/build/

